WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:14.740
(Watch on KonFlix.vip)

00:00:03.852 --> 00:00:04.820
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.221
(All characters, organizations, and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:00:06.221 --> 00:00:07.289
(Scenes with child actors followed production guidelines.)

00:00:11.568 --> 00:00:14.638
So a proposal came up from Yeonri-ri?

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:16.606
Yes, I'll handle it myself.

00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:18.942
You know...

00:00:19.576 --> 00:00:22.312
I find that kind of story very interesting.

00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:25.382
A stubborn person who only knows one way...

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:28.118
experiences frustration and falls apart.

00:00:31.722 --> 00:00:34.624
Seeing what choice he makes in that moment...

00:00:34.925 --> 00:00:36.760
Isn't that what life is really about?

00:00:46.369 --> 00:00:47.571
Chief, I...

00:00:48.605 --> 00:00:50.974
I'm sorry, Chief. Please help me.

00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:51.808
Chief.

00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:53.877
It's for the company, right?

00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:55.645
Call them up.

00:00:57.013 --> 00:00:58.582
Or just do the research you want.

00:01:03.854 --> 00:01:04.855
Chief.

00:01:13.597 --> 00:01:17.601
But there's no way he'll actually succeed, right?

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:20.771
No way.

00:01:21.405 --> 00:01:23.306
Why do you think Yeonri-ri is called a place of exile?

00:01:23.974 --> 00:01:25.442
Still, just in case...

00:01:25.742 --> 00:01:28.211
I introduced a small variable.

00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:53.837
Yes, Mr. Choi.

00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:56.740
Mr. Seong? How are things over there?

00:01:57.007 --> 00:02:00.377
Well... Things are going well.

00:02:00.377 --> 00:02:02.045
Did you see the proposal?

00:02:02.045 --> 00:02:03.780
To grow the seedlings, I need a budget...

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.148
But as you already know,

00:02:05.148 --> 00:02:08.151
the headquarters' budget is tight right now.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:11.088
So increasing the budget will be difficult.

00:02:11.722 --> 00:02:15.525
But I'll report the seedling matter to the executive director personally.

00:02:15.525 --> 00:02:16.359
What?

00:02:16.626 --> 00:02:18.562
Within one month, send seedling samples.

00:02:18.562 --> 00:02:20.464
I want 300 of each sample,

00:02:20.764 --> 00:02:22.399
so 1,500 total.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:24.768
In one month?

00:02:24.768 --> 00:02:26.002
Fifteen hundred seedlings?

00:02:26.002 --> 00:02:28.438
If I send 1,500 seedlings to headquarters,

00:02:28.438 --> 00:02:31.708
I won't have enough left to plant napa cabbage here.

00:02:31.708 --> 00:02:34.244
And I need at least a month and a half.

00:02:34.244 --> 00:02:35.245
Really?

00:02:35.746 --> 00:02:37.981
Then you'll just need to plant more.

00:02:37.981 --> 00:02:40.250
One month? Or as soon as possible?

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.952
Okay. Keep up the good work.

00:02:45.322 --> 00:02:46.590
Hello?

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:56.500
(EP 2 Even When Tears Well Up, Look Up)

00:02:58.802 --> 00:03:00.036
It's cold.

00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:07.844
One on one?

00:03:07.844 --> 00:03:09.413
No, it's too expensive.

00:03:11.214 --> 00:03:12.149
Mom.

00:03:12.149 --> 00:03:13.450
When are we going back to Seoul?

00:03:13.984 --> 00:03:15.519
It's not that easy.

00:03:15.519 --> 00:03:16.453
Look.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.623
There's no Wi-Fi! No Wi-Fi!

00:03:19.623 --> 00:03:21.925
Do you think money just falls from the sky?

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:25.762
We can't even sell our house in Canada right now.

00:03:28.331 --> 00:03:30.467
Simwoo Elementary School.

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:34.104
Simwoo Elementary and Middle School?

00:03:34.671 --> 00:03:36.339
The elementary and middle schools are combined?

00:03:39.342 --> 00:03:42.012
Five elementary students and five middle school students?

00:03:42.846 --> 00:03:45.215
Not five per class,

00:03:45.215 --> 00:03:47.250
but five in the entire school? Only ten students in total?

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.292
It's only temporary,

00:03:55.292 --> 00:03:57.928
so you're okay with going to a nearby school, right?

00:03:58.361 --> 00:03:59.629
I'm okay.

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:01.631
No! I don't want to.

00:04:01.865 --> 00:04:03.700
If it's not for long, do I really have to go to school?

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:04.534
Yes.

00:04:04.835 --> 00:04:07.904
Seong Ji Sang. You definitely have to go.

00:04:07.904 --> 00:04:09.973
If you come last again, you're dead meat.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.591
What's this?

00:04:27.891 --> 00:04:30.494
- Dad, something smells weird. - What is this?

00:04:30.494 --> 00:04:32.162
What? What happened?

00:04:35.132 --> 00:04:36.933
Water shot up from the ground.

00:04:36.933 --> 00:04:37.901
What?

00:04:38.068 --> 00:04:40.971
This darn land has ruined us.

00:04:41.738 --> 00:04:42.672
Honey.

00:04:45.275 --> 00:04:47.577
"Messed up" is standard language.

00:04:48.211 --> 00:04:49.312
Don't step on the carpet, honey.

00:04:49.746 --> 00:04:51.481
The first meaning is "to ruin something."

00:04:51.481 --> 00:04:53.483
The second meaning is "to beat someone up."

00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:54.518
That's what it means.

00:04:54.518 --> 00:04:56.019
Your footprints. Come on.

00:04:56.019 --> 00:04:57.888
Ji Sang, go open the door. The door. The door.

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:00.424
Everyone, listen up.

00:05:00.757 --> 00:05:03.193
Someone from Mat Story has come to our village.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.362
He was demoted and sent here.

00:05:05.362 --> 00:05:06.930
I thought he'd go back after a few days,

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:09.533
but now he says he's going to grow napa cabbage.

00:05:09.533 --> 00:05:11.301
He even named it "Seong Tae Hun cabbage" after himself.

00:05:11.735 --> 00:05:12.936
Napa cabbage?

00:05:12.936 --> 00:05:14.638
They're doing that again?

00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:18.041
I'd rather have dirt thrown in my eyes.

00:05:18.041 --> 00:05:20.077
Mat Story is unbelievable.

00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:22.546
You remember what they did before, right?

00:05:22.813 --> 00:05:27.017
They made a huge fuss about using a tiny bit of pesticide,

00:05:27.017 --> 00:05:30.353
and ended up canceling all the contracts, right?

00:05:30.353 --> 00:05:31.888
How much did you lose back then?

00:05:31.888 --> 00:05:33.290
Don't even ask.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:35.258
- He lost a lot. - He lost everything, right?

00:05:35.258 --> 00:05:37.360
I officially declare this...

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.595
as the village chief.

00:05:38.795 --> 00:05:42.232
Do not help Seong Tae Hun at all.

00:05:42.632 --> 00:05:44.468
- You got that? - All right. All right.

00:05:44.468 --> 00:05:45.335
Okay.

00:05:48.038 --> 00:05:48.805
Especially...

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.742
Wang Dong Sik.

00:05:51.742 --> 00:05:52.709
Yes?

00:05:52.709 --> 00:05:54.678
He'll definitely go to your hardware store.

00:05:55.078 --> 00:05:56.580
No matter how much he begs,

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.715
you must not help him. Got it?

00:05:58.715 --> 00:06:00.350
He's too soft-hearted.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.052
If he feels even a little sorry,

00:06:02.052 --> 00:06:03.887
he'll run right over with his tools.

00:06:03.887 --> 00:06:04.688
That's right.

00:06:04.688 --> 00:06:06.356
When did I ever do that?

00:06:07.257 --> 00:06:09.726
I'm a tough guy.

00:06:10.594 --> 00:06:11.495
He's really coming.

00:06:12.062 --> 00:06:13.730
He doesn't look so good.

00:06:14.164 --> 00:06:15.799
Fixing drainage pipes isn't something just anyone can do.

00:06:15.799 --> 00:06:17.601
You're really going to make him fix it by himself?

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:20.170
But that could end up flooding your field too.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.906
You're too nice.

00:06:22.906 --> 00:06:24.408
Have you forgotten...

00:06:24.408 --> 00:06:26.510
how Mat Story treated us before?

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.044
Yes, I know. I do, but...

00:06:28.044 --> 00:06:29.913
But it's not that easy to ignore someone.

00:06:29.913 --> 00:06:31.381
He's coming.

00:06:31.648 --> 00:06:33.483
What am I going to do? Goodbye.

00:06:34.918 --> 00:06:37.587
(Wang Dong Hardware)

00:06:37.587 --> 00:06:38.855
I need a drill.

00:06:40.791 --> 00:06:42.959
Hello. This is Wang Dong Hardware.

00:06:45.562 --> 00:06:48.398
I'm in big trouble with water.

00:06:49.599 --> 00:06:50.700
Please help me out, Mr. Wang.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:52.502
Please.

00:06:52.769 --> 00:06:53.770
You...

00:06:54.438 --> 00:06:56.339
are in big trouble with water.

00:07:15.525 --> 00:07:18.962
Well, as I already told you,

00:07:18.962 --> 00:07:22.099
if I go out there myself, it'll be quite costly.

00:07:27.604 --> 00:07:31.074
Here, I just deliver supplies,

00:07:31.074 --> 00:07:34.945
and the owner fixes things himself. That's how things work around here.

00:07:34.945 --> 00:07:36.346
That's how it is.

00:07:36.913 --> 00:07:39.850
But you'll at least tell me how to fix it, right?

00:07:40.417 --> 00:07:43.220
Well... How to fix it...

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:44.855
Don't ever do it for free.

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:46.532
Be sure to get paid properly.

00:07:46.999 --> 00:07:47.800
Of course.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.903
Yes, of course. I know how valuable technical skills are.

00:07:51.237 --> 00:07:53.306
I'll pay you the amount you quoted right away.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:55.675
Please provide me with a receipt, though.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.777
- A receipt. - Okay.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:03.749
Unload the stuff right now.

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:05.318
Okay. Okay.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:14.493
Even planting a single seed takes skill,

00:08:14.493 --> 00:08:15.728
but people don't know that.

00:08:16.162 --> 00:08:18.664
They think country people do everything for free.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:19.899
But that's not true.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:20.766
Are you listening to me?

00:08:32.044 --> 00:08:32.945
Let's do this.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.455
Meat, meat, meat.

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.823
Chief meat.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:45.658
Flip it over.

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:54.100
Do a good job.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:56.902
Think of it as method acting.

00:08:56.902 --> 00:08:58.904
- Method. - You're good at it, right?

00:08:58.904 --> 00:08:59.772
Hey.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.774
Goodness.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.044
Protein in the morning.

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:06.779
This is like medicine, right?

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:08.547
This is amazing.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:09.582
- Isn't it amazing? - Yes.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:12.051
I'm cutting it now. Here it goes.

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:12.985
My heart is racing.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:16.622
Take a bite.

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:19.725
- We eat like this every day. - That looks good.

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:22.128
This...

00:09:22.128 --> 00:09:24.497
It has to be smoking like this.

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:27.166
Thank you. I'm full already this morning.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.873
Why is the road so narrow? I'm afraid I'll crash my car.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.344
Seong Ji Sang.

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:41.514
If you cause trouble again, you really have nowhere else to go.

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:46.719
Shoot.

00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:48.688
What kind of school is this?

00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:50.656
This school sucks.

00:09:50.656 --> 00:09:53.125
You'll be transferring soon anyway, so just hang in there.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.094
Lighten up.

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:57.530
Let's go.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:09:59.565
Let's go, Ji Gu.

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.669
Welcome.

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:06.772
Say hello.

00:10:06.772 --> 00:10:07.873
Say hello.

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:09.976
Hello.

00:10:09.976 --> 00:10:11.043
Welcome.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.286
So the kids from Seoul aren't that special.

00:10:20.286 --> 00:10:21.220
Exactly.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:23.089
Is he a loser?

00:10:23.089 --> 00:10:24.590
His mom is dropping him off at school.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:28.928
Guys.

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:31.731
Be quiet, okay?

00:10:32.999 --> 00:10:35.768
Thank you all for coming out to greet us.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:38.638
The two of you, come this way.

00:10:38.638 --> 00:10:40.339
Let's go inside.

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:41.440
Let's go inside.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.908
Let's go inside.

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:45.478
Hey. What are you doing?

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:47.446
Are you crying because you miss your mom?

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:49.882
Look up.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.652
Too bad you can't go home.

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:02.695
(Elementary School Sprout Class)

00:11:02.695 --> 00:11:03.763
Hello.

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:05.698
My name is Ji Gu.

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:07.600
Where do you come from?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.735
Whatcha saying? What's wrong with ya?

00:11:11.304 --> 00:11:13.005
What language is that?

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:16.609
There's a groove in the socket.

00:11:16.609 --> 00:11:19.145
Match this part and tighten the pipe.

00:11:19.145 --> 00:11:20.846
Then use a screwdriver on both sides...

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:24.583
Be gentle.

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:26.352
Or it'll burst again.

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:30.623
Unbelievable.

00:11:36.329 --> 00:11:38.564
I heard the village chief in Tuchang-ri passed away.

00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:41.400
When are you going to the funeral?

00:11:42.435 --> 00:11:44.036
I'll go home to get changed and then go.

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:45.304
- What about you? - Me?

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.742
Yes. Me too.

00:11:52.345 --> 00:11:53.679
Right.

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:56.716
I have to go to Daegu to pick up some supplies today.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:58.951
I totally forgot.

00:11:59.885 --> 00:12:02.588
Forget it. I'm sure he'd understand.

00:12:02.922 --> 00:12:04.323
The living must keep living.

00:12:08.394 --> 00:12:10.663
That's it for today.

00:12:10.663 --> 00:12:12.832
Just continue the rest tomorrow.

00:12:19.472 --> 00:12:20.506
I should get going now.

00:12:36.055 --> 00:12:38.357
(Academic advisor)

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:51.203
Dr. Seong.

00:12:52.838 --> 00:12:53.839
Did you get some rest?

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.409
Medical school is tough, isn't it?

00:12:56.409 --> 00:12:58.210
It's okay.

00:13:00.346 --> 00:13:02.882
You're so grown-up.

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:06.452
Even when things get hard, you never complain.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.688
I'm so proud of you.

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:13.125
I'm off to pick up the kids from school.

00:13:13.125 --> 00:13:14.360
Are you craving anything to eat?

00:13:14.827 --> 00:13:16.829
No, I'm fine. You should go.

00:13:42.521 --> 00:13:43.622
Who is it at this hour?

00:13:50.329 --> 00:13:53.199
Mr. Wang, what are you doing here?

00:13:53.199 --> 00:13:55.134
We have to hurry. We don't have a lot of time.

00:13:55.134 --> 00:13:56.202
Time?

00:13:56.202 --> 00:13:57.370
- Let's go. Let's go. - Okay.

00:14:01.774 --> 00:14:02.608
A drill.

00:14:16.022 --> 00:14:16.956
Turn on the water.

00:14:21.227 --> 00:14:23.929
What's wrong with this? What's going on?

00:14:24.263 --> 00:14:25.464
What's going on here?

00:14:26.432 --> 00:14:27.400
This is bad.

00:14:28.134 --> 00:14:29.568
Turn it off. Turn it off.

00:14:31.604 --> 00:14:32.905
The pipes have been rotting for so long...

00:14:32.905 --> 00:14:34.774
that when you fix one side, another one bursts open.

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:39.445
Come on, hose. Let's see who wins.

00:14:41.147 --> 00:14:43.382
He always said...

00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:44.483
Yes.

00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:47.086
"You have to protect Yeonri-ri."

00:14:47.086 --> 00:14:48.020
Hye Sun.

00:14:48.354 --> 00:14:51.757
What is a village chief? It's all about power.

00:14:51.757 --> 00:14:52.792
Right.

00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:55.594
This whole time, you used that power...

00:14:55.995 --> 00:14:57.596
to open soju bottles.

00:14:58.564 --> 00:14:59.398
Hold this.

00:15:06.839 --> 00:15:07.707
Let's move on.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:14.213
- Mr. Seong. - It's on. It's on. It's on.

00:15:14.213 --> 00:15:16.649
Please, hose. Come on.

00:15:16.649 --> 00:15:18.517
Come on.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:21.053
It's not leaking. It's not leaking.

00:15:23.222 --> 00:15:24.890
It's not leaking, Mr. Seong.

00:15:25.624 --> 00:15:28.160
It's not leaking. It's not leaking.

00:15:31.897 --> 00:15:32.932
That's great.

00:15:34.674 --> 00:15:37.503
Everything is about skill.

00:15:37.503 --> 00:15:39.438
You can't ever beat a professional.

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:42.908
Well...

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:45.311
I'm sure the company didn't give you money when they exiled you here.

00:15:46.078 --> 00:15:48.614
You're spending your own money, so why did you pay me so much?

00:15:49.015 --> 00:15:52.284
I guess because I spent my whole life researching napa cabbage,

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:53.919
I can't cut corners on things like this.

00:15:53.919 --> 00:15:54.754
Seriously...

00:15:55.921 --> 00:15:56.889
Thank you so much.

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:00.726
I'm sure you helped me...

00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:03.496
because if the water leaks, it'll flood the chief's field too.

00:16:03.496 --> 00:16:04.563
Even so...

00:16:04.563 --> 00:16:07.333
Goodness. You're not completely clueless.

00:16:09.902 --> 00:16:12.972
Try to stand on your own now.

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:13.906
Hye Sun.

00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:19.011
When I touch you, you might burst...

00:16:19.812 --> 00:16:20.813
What's that?

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:22.114
What?

00:16:22.882 --> 00:16:23.783
Over there.

00:16:25.851 --> 00:16:27.486
- Isn't that the Mat Story's field? - What?

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:32.525
What's going on over there?

00:16:33.326 --> 00:16:34.860
Why is it so bright over there? Hold on.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:37.063
- Careful or you'll fall. - Wang Dong Sik.

00:16:38.197 --> 00:16:40.800
So... About the village chief...

00:16:41.367 --> 00:16:43.302
He's not such a terrible person.

00:16:44.904 --> 00:16:46.138
Wang Dong Sik.

00:16:46.939 --> 00:16:47.873
Wang Dong Sik.

00:16:47.873 --> 00:16:50.509
It's the chief. Run!

00:16:50.509 --> 00:16:53.612
Hide in the office. Hide in the office.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.748
Hurry. Come on.

00:16:55.748 --> 00:16:57.917
You did this all by yourself. All by yourself.

00:16:59.385 --> 00:17:00.653
Chief.

00:17:00.653 --> 00:17:01.854
You'll fall.

00:17:11.397 --> 00:17:12.732
Chief.

00:17:12.732 --> 00:17:14.233
Did you go somewhere?

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.006
Wang Dong Sik, that soft tofu punk.

00:17:20.006 --> 00:17:21.140
Where is Wang Dong Sik?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.475
You're starting to scare me.

00:17:22.475 --> 00:17:24.243
Is there a ghost or something?

00:17:24.243 --> 00:17:26.278
I've been here all by myself this whole time.

00:17:26.278 --> 00:17:27.747
There were two lights.

00:17:28.981 --> 00:17:31.317
There's one here and another one over there.

00:17:31.317 --> 00:17:34.820
I can't see anything at night, so I turned on two lights.

00:17:36.622 --> 00:17:37.723
Chief? Where are you going?

00:17:38.491 --> 00:17:39.358
Chief?

00:17:39.859 --> 00:17:41.694
He's coming this way. My goodness.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:45.798
Well...

00:17:47.533 --> 00:17:48.434
I...

00:17:53.372 --> 00:17:54.307
Where are you?

00:17:55.841 --> 00:17:56.742
Wang Dong Sik.

00:17:58.611 --> 00:17:59.545
Wang Dong Sik.

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:01.814
Wang Dong Sik.

00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:29.642
If you run the generator like that at night,

00:18:29.642 --> 00:18:31.310
how are people supposed to sleep?

00:18:32.178 --> 00:18:33.579
Even the hens won't lay eggs!

00:18:34.647 --> 00:18:37.149
Let's go, okay? Let's go now.

00:18:37.516 --> 00:18:38.484
Goodness.

00:18:39.085 --> 00:18:42.855
The hens have to lay eggs if we want fried eggs.

00:18:43.322 --> 00:18:47.226
- Right. - You know how much he loved fried eggs.

00:18:47.226 --> 00:18:50.396
He would fry and eat many eggs a day.

00:18:50.396 --> 00:18:51.564
That's right.

00:18:51.564 --> 00:18:53.432
- Protein is good for you. - He's gone.

00:18:53.432 --> 00:18:55.034
- I... - You're okay. You're okay.

00:18:55.468 --> 00:18:56.335
What a relief.

00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:05.978
Send seedling samples within one month. Fifteen hundred total.

00:19:07.346 --> 00:19:09.715
(D-day)

00:19:09.715 --> 00:19:10.950
(Yeonri-ri Project 1. Fix the field drainage)

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:13.019
(2. Clear the field)

00:19:13.285 --> 00:19:14.286
I can do this.

00:19:15.721 --> 00:19:16.689
I can do this.

00:19:34.774 --> 00:19:36.709
He seems to be excited after fixing the drainage problem.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.446
Whether you remove the rocks or roll them away, that's all you'll do.

00:19:41.747 --> 00:19:43.416
You'll need fertilizer next, right?

00:19:44.684 --> 00:19:46.085
Not a chance.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.555
(2. Clear the field)

00:19:49.555 --> 00:19:51.824
(3. Get compost and fertilizer)

00:19:51.824 --> 00:19:52.758
(Simwoo-myeon Community Center)

00:19:52.758 --> 00:19:54.427
If you want to apply for the fertilizer supply,

00:19:54.427 --> 00:19:56.829
you need to submit a usage report first.

00:19:56.829 --> 00:19:58.264
(Village chief stamp required)

00:19:58.264 --> 00:20:01.167
Be sure to get the village chief's approval stamp.

00:20:01.701 --> 00:20:03.002
The village chief?

00:20:03.002 --> 00:20:04.670
We can't proceed without his stamp.

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:06.439
Okay. Thank you.

00:20:11.577 --> 00:20:13.813
Chief, I sent him away.

00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:17.116
You can't participate in the fertilizer group purchase unless you're a member.

00:20:18.184 --> 00:20:19.852
Bring a recommendation from the village chief.

00:20:23.522 --> 00:20:24.724
Here...

00:20:24.724 --> 00:20:25.858
All by yourself...

00:20:26.325 --> 00:20:28.627
What do you think you can do?

00:20:30.429 --> 00:20:32.732
I'll smack you.

00:20:35.701 --> 00:20:37.703
Chief, mission complete.

00:20:37.703 --> 00:20:39.805
I will not lose this time.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:44.610
(Pesticide Farm Supply Store)

00:20:45.845 --> 00:20:46.712
Sir.

00:20:47.847 --> 00:20:50.883
I'd like to buy two 20-kg bags of urea fertilizer.

00:20:50.883 --> 00:20:52.018
Please.

00:20:52.018 --> 00:20:53.953
They're sold out.

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:57.657
Then what about all those bags piled up over there?

00:20:57.657 --> 00:20:58.691
Reserved orders.

00:20:58.924 --> 00:20:59.825
Even if I had some,

00:20:59.825 --> 00:21:03.062
you can't get them without the village chief's stamp.

00:21:03.996 --> 00:21:05.097
Village chief.

00:21:05.097 --> 00:21:06.966
Village chief.

00:21:11.537 --> 00:21:13.306
Chief, mission complete.

00:21:14.173 --> 00:21:16.242
A spy.

00:21:23.349 --> 00:21:24.917
(Maweo Horticultural Complex)

00:21:28.187 --> 00:21:32.458
I will make sure you can't do anything here.

00:21:34.026 --> 00:21:36.529
That darn chief.

00:21:40.566 --> 00:21:41.400
Okay.

00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:44.303
Let me try to find some emotional content.

00:21:53.546 --> 00:21:56.115
This tree looks nice.

00:21:56.782 --> 00:21:59.018
I got it.

00:21:59.018 --> 00:22:00.920
This is it.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.927
Taking a break from the intense life in Toronto...

00:22:07.927 --> 00:22:08.961
with my kids.

00:22:10.029 --> 00:22:11.497
Sharp phytoncide.

00:22:11.497 --> 00:22:13.199
Sharp in nature.

00:22:28.447 --> 00:22:29.815
It's so dusty.

00:22:43.763 --> 00:22:44.997
How dirty.

00:22:52.838 --> 00:22:53.839
Dr. Seong.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:55.608
Are you heading out?

00:22:56.042 --> 00:22:56.876
What?

00:22:57.109 --> 00:22:58.044
You see...

00:22:58.844 --> 00:22:59.979
I'm going out to study.

00:23:01.714 --> 00:23:03.115
School hasn't started yet?

00:23:03.115 --> 00:23:04.383
When are you going back?

00:23:04.383 --> 00:23:05.718
Well...

00:23:05.718 --> 00:23:07.219
Even after the semester starts,

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:10.156
it's a pre-clerkship self-study block.

00:23:10.389 --> 00:23:14.460
So it's the same whether I study at the library or at home.

00:23:15.428 --> 00:23:16.896
Is there such a thing?

00:23:16.896 --> 00:23:18.097
That's great.

00:23:18.731 --> 00:23:20.366
I should go study.

00:23:20.967 --> 00:23:22.468
Okay. See you later.

00:23:28.808 --> 00:23:29.909
Is she not here today?

00:23:35.081 --> 00:23:36.015
Anyone here?

00:23:36.749 --> 00:23:37.616
Bo Mi.

00:23:52.565 --> 00:23:54.300
Bo Mi?

00:24:01.941 --> 00:24:04.644
What? Do you like older women?

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:09.815
- Please excuse me. - Here you go.

00:24:12.251 --> 00:24:13.419
You look so pretty.

00:24:14.754 --> 00:24:16.522
Thank you. Thank you.

00:24:16.789 --> 00:24:18.324
Have some berry tea before you go.

00:24:18.891 --> 00:24:20.393
Hey, tall boy. Come here.

00:24:22.995 --> 00:24:24.130
(Menu of the month)

00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:25.931
(Today's menu, brown rice, cucumber kimchi, blueberry yogurt)

00:24:42.682 --> 00:24:43.683
Food.

00:24:43.683 --> 00:24:45.584
Food. It looks good.

00:24:49.388 --> 00:24:50.389
Serve the soup.

00:24:52.158 --> 00:24:54.894
Slowly. One at a time. If you run, you won't get any.

00:24:54.894 --> 00:24:57.096
Come here. You must be hungry.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:58.431
Come in.

00:25:02.702 --> 00:25:03.669
Go first.

00:25:07.840 --> 00:25:10.242
Where in Seoul are you from?

00:25:15.481 --> 00:25:17.450
I don't need any friends and I have a girlfriend.

00:25:17.683 --> 00:25:19.652
I got expelled for beating up a guy who messed with me.

00:25:20.853 --> 00:25:22.288
So don't bother me.

00:25:29.595 --> 00:25:32.298
I got expelled for beating up a guy who messed with me.

00:25:33.132 --> 00:25:33.966
Crazy.

00:25:35.434 --> 00:25:36.502
Have you lost your mind?

00:25:36.969 --> 00:25:40.139
You're making me cringe. Are you shooting a soap opera?

00:25:40.139 --> 00:25:41.674
You're so cute.

00:25:47.146 --> 00:25:48.781
This was a gift from Carol.

00:25:48.781 --> 00:25:50.116
What do I do?

00:25:50.116 --> 00:25:51.484
Hey, Canada.

00:25:52.118 --> 00:25:53.252
Did you just swear at me?

00:25:54.854 --> 00:25:56.656
I didn't before, but I am now.

00:25:57.189 --> 00:25:58.791
You punk!

00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:10.903
My nose is bleeding!

00:26:14.373 --> 00:26:15.841
Come here, you jerk.

00:26:17.176 --> 00:26:18.010
Come here.

00:26:20.046 --> 00:26:21.547
Get lost, punk.

00:26:23.649 --> 00:26:24.550
Hey.

00:26:26.852 --> 00:26:27.687
Let go.

00:26:28.587 --> 00:26:29.855
Let go.

00:26:29.855 --> 00:26:31.924
Stop fighting, Ji Sang.

00:26:33.459 --> 00:26:34.427
Stop.

00:26:35.761 --> 00:26:38.297
Who's throwing punches in the sacred cafeteria?

00:26:40.633 --> 00:26:42.735
You don't want to eat lunch?

00:26:43.536 --> 00:26:44.470
Let go.

00:26:50.710 --> 00:26:52.278
Don't waste your energy on useless stuff.

00:26:52.278 --> 00:26:54.213
You're at school, okay?

00:26:55.147 --> 00:26:56.115
Stop this and go back inside.

00:27:04.557 --> 00:27:06.092
Come on.

00:27:06.892 --> 00:27:08.928
This is your favorite side dish.

00:27:08.928 --> 00:27:10.830
- Enjoy. - Thank you.

00:27:11.697 --> 00:27:12.598
Enjoy.

00:27:14.367 --> 00:27:16.402
What is this?

00:27:16.402 --> 00:27:18.938
This is seasoned taro stem.

00:27:18.938 --> 00:27:20.840
The texture is interesting, and it's good. Try it.

00:27:24.443 --> 00:27:25.911
Would you like some more?

00:27:25.911 --> 00:27:26.746
No?

00:27:46.999 --> 00:27:49.435
What? I'm not eating.

00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:53.572
This was made with ingredients the kids grew themselves,

00:27:53.572 --> 00:27:54.640
so it's on another level.

00:27:55.207 --> 00:27:56.275
Come on.

00:28:31.210 --> 00:28:32.511
My goodness.

00:28:38.117 --> 00:28:39.051
Hello.

00:28:39.852 --> 00:28:40.720
Sir.

00:28:42.321 --> 00:28:44.857
You're out even in this heat. You're still very healthy.

00:28:44.857 --> 00:28:45.992
Thank you for your hard work.

00:28:46.525 --> 00:28:47.393
Ma'am.

00:28:47.860 --> 00:28:50.329
Even if it's uncomfortable, you must wear a helmet.

00:28:50.963 --> 00:28:51.864
Hello.

00:29:10.716 --> 00:29:13.986
(Cafe Sunny)

00:29:19.859 --> 00:29:22.028
- Hello. - You're here.

00:29:22.028 --> 00:29:24.263
Iced Americano with an extra shot. Large.

00:29:24.263 --> 00:29:25.131
Thank you.

00:29:27.633 --> 00:29:29.135
Bo Mi reported...

00:29:29.135 --> 00:29:32.071
a broken streetlight near the bridge the other day.

00:29:32.071 --> 00:29:33.806
Please tell her it's been fixed.

00:29:33.806 --> 00:29:35.308
You did good work.

00:29:35.308 --> 00:29:36.475
No.

00:29:36.909 --> 00:29:39.345
Seon Ja. Let's go...

00:29:39.345 --> 00:29:41.347
deliver coffee to school tomorrow.

00:29:41.347 --> 00:29:42.214
Okay.

00:29:42.948 --> 00:29:44.150
Do you want me to go?

00:29:44.684 --> 00:29:47.353
It's on my patrol route anyway, so I can go.

00:29:47.353 --> 00:29:48.587
That's okay.

00:29:48.587 --> 00:29:52.358
I'm sure you are very busy too.

00:29:53.225 --> 00:29:54.493
Here you go.

00:29:54.493 --> 00:29:57.129
Officer Park, ice refills are free for you.

00:29:57.496 --> 00:29:58.331
You know?

00:29:58.631 --> 00:29:59.699
- Thank you. - Sure.

00:29:59.699 --> 00:30:00.700
Goodbye.

00:30:00.700 --> 00:30:02.201
- Bye. - Bye, officer.

00:30:02.201 --> 00:30:03.235
Bye.

00:30:04.670 --> 00:30:05.705
Goodbye.

00:30:06.372 --> 00:30:07.873
Goodbye.

00:30:10.042 --> 00:30:11.110
- Bye. - Bye.

00:30:12.044 --> 00:30:14.246
If he likes Bo Mi that much,

00:30:14.613 --> 00:30:16.015
why doesn't he confess his love to her?

00:30:30.429 --> 00:30:31.330
That hurts.

00:31:01.293 --> 00:31:03.262
Can you pick up the kids?

00:31:03.262 --> 00:31:05.097
The school bus broke down.

00:31:12.638 --> 00:31:15.007
Is this it? Is there anything else I can do for you?

00:31:15.007 --> 00:31:18.277
Wipe your sweat before you say that.

00:31:18.277 --> 00:31:21.113
You're struggling every day with that tiny body of yours.

00:31:21.714 --> 00:31:22.748
Come on.

00:31:23.115 --> 00:31:25.685
I was born with a farming spoon in Yeonri-ri.

00:31:26.185 --> 00:31:28.220
Instead of you doing all the work,

00:31:28.587 --> 00:31:31.290
can't we just hire one more young worker?

00:31:31.757 --> 00:31:33.292
I want to do that as well.

00:31:33.292 --> 00:31:34.627
I really want to,

00:31:34.627 --> 00:31:36.629
but no matter how hard I look,

00:31:36.629 --> 00:31:38.097
the only young worker here is...

00:31:39.365 --> 00:31:41.500
me, Im Bo Mi.

00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:42.868
Come on.

00:31:42.868 --> 00:31:45.638
Forget it. Let's go home now.

00:31:46.605 --> 00:31:47.907
I'll work like 100 people again tomorrow.

00:31:47.907 --> 00:31:49.075
Okay. Bye.

00:32:08.494 --> 00:32:09.729
Bo Mi.

00:32:09.729 --> 00:32:10.730
Officer Park.

00:32:12.098 --> 00:32:14.900
You're out on patrol just when it's time for the kids to go home, right?

00:32:15.301 --> 00:32:16.669
I'm just doing my job.

00:32:16.902 --> 00:32:19.071
Even so, thank you so much.

00:32:19.071 --> 00:32:21.407
It's a beautiful day today, isn't it?

00:32:21.407 --> 00:32:22.341
Yes.

00:32:29.448 --> 00:32:31.751
Mr. Seong Ji Cheon.

00:32:37.490 --> 00:32:38.824
- It's Bo Mi. - Do you know him?

00:32:38.824 --> 00:32:39.759
Bo Mi.

00:32:40.459 --> 00:32:42.328
He moved here recently.

00:32:49.535 --> 00:32:50.936
What brings you here?

00:32:51.137 --> 00:32:53.639
I'm here to pick up my brothers.

00:32:54.073 --> 00:32:56.842
You must be the older brother of those new students.

00:32:56.842 --> 00:32:58.344
You know my brothers?

00:33:01.213 --> 00:33:02.281
You're from Seoul?

00:33:03.516 --> 00:33:04.984
I'm Officer Park Soon Kyung.

00:33:05.384 --> 00:33:06.352
Easy to remember, right?

00:33:08.821 --> 00:33:09.922
If anything happens,

00:33:09.922 --> 00:33:12.091
come to the Yeonri-ri police substation and ask for me.

00:33:14.960 --> 00:33:15.795
Okay.

00:33:30.042 --> 00:33:30.910
Ji Sang Gu.

00:33:31.711 --> 00:33:34.113
What? I'm so angry.

00:33:38.751 --> 00:33:40.820
What? Were you in a fight again?

00:33:42.088 --> 00:33:43.756
I can take care of myself.

00:33:43.756 --> 00:33:45.257
If you cause trouble again, you're dead meat.

00:33:47.526 --> 00:33:48.394
Let's go say hello.

00:33:50.162 --> 00:33:51.530
- Hi. - Hello.

00:33:51.530 --> 00:33:52.365
Hi.

00:33:54.333 --> 00:33:56.502
Ma'am. Do you know my older brother?

00:33:58.204 --> 00:33:59.472
Yes, I do.

00:34:00.940 --> 00:34:03.776
Are you famous for being a Hangook University medical student?

00:34:05.878 --> 00:34:08.881
I've never met a med student before.

00:34:08.881 --> 00:34:09.815
How cool.

00:34:09.815 --> 00:34:10.716
I'm not.

00:34:12.184 --> 00:34:14.353
That's not what I meant.

00:34:15.087 --> 00:34:17.556
I came here to take a break from it.

00:34:19.025 --> 00:34:20.526
We'll get going now.

00:34:21.727 --> 00:34:23.796
- So you're not a med student? - Yes, I am.

00:34:24.630 --> 00:34:25.598
- Goodbye. - What was that?

00:34:25.598 --> 00:34:27.433
It's nothing. I am a med student.

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:29.402
Are you really?

00:34:29.802 --> 00:34:31.003
Yes.

00:34:31.003 --> 00:34:32.872
- You're not, are you? - I am.

00:34:33.139 --> 00:34:35.074
I don't think you are.

00:34:35.074 --> 00:34:35.908
I am.

00:34:37.910 --> 00:34:38.844
If you're not?

00:34:39.712 --> 00:34:40.946
What do you do then?

00:34:40.946 --> 00:34:41.681
What?

00:34:43.883 --> 00:34:45.117
I just...

00:34:45.818 --> 00:34:47.787
This and that...

00:34:48.688 --> 00:34:49.588
I have a lot on my mind.

00:34:50.156 --> 00:34:52.325
Do you know what's best when you have a lot on your mind?

00:34:53.926 --> 00:34:54.794
I don't know.

00:34:55.461 --> 00:34:57.096
You must use your body.

00:34:57.096 --> 00:34:58.798
- My body? - Yes.

00:35:02.401 --> 00:35:03.269
Give me your number.

00:35:41.007 --> 00:35:42.341
(Manufactured date, November 2018)

00:35:42.341 --> 00:35:43.743
(Expiration date, two years from the manufactured date)

00:35:46.579 --> 00:35:47.847
Let's find a way.

00:35:48.648 --> 00:35:51.250
If there's no proper way, I'll find another way.

00:36:08.567 --> 00:36:12.204
(3. Get compost and fertilizer)

00:36:16.409 --> 00:36:17.276
Look at him.

00:36:18.044 --> 00:36:19.278
One bag won't be enough.

00:36:22.114 --> 00:36:23.683
The ignorant are brave.

00:36:24.350 --> 00:36:26.986
What if he falls over while doing that?

00:36:26.986 --> 00:36:28.387
I should go over there,

00:36:28.387 --> 00:36:30.389
and tell him to rest.

00:36:32.091 --> 00:36:34.093
He'll rest when he's tired. Leave him be.

00:36:34.093 --> 00:36:35.194
Why are you meddling?

00:36:35.995 --> 00:36:39.098
Mak Rae, stop minding him and eat your sweet potato, okay?

00:36:40.733 --> 00:36:44.003
But doesn't he seem to be sincere?

00:36:44.270 --> 00:36:45.438
Look at him.

00:36:45.438 --> 00:36:47.673
He even spent his own money to fix the drainage.

00:36:48.007 --> 00:36:48.874
True.

00:36:49.108 --> 00:36:52.178
He's the first guy who actually plowed that land.

00:36:52.378 --> 00:36:54.547
Look at him.

00:36:54.547 --> 00:36:57.616
He is pretty handsome,

00:36:57.616 --> 00:36:58.918
and tall.

00:36:58.918 --> 00:37:00.453
He has broad shoulders,

00:37:00.453 --> 00:37:01.854
and a strong build.

00:37:01.854 --> 00:37:05.091
He looks really strong.

00:37:05.958 --> 00:37:06.926
How did he end up like this?

00:37:07.994 --> 00:37:10.863
Mak Rae, snap out of it.

00:37:11.263 --> 00:37:13.532
Anyone who helps him out...

00:37:13.532 --> 00:37:15.267
will become an outcast in Yeonri-ri.

00:37:19.105 --> 00:37:20.239
Who do you think you are?

00:37:20.706 --> 00:37:23.109
People in Korea have freedom of residence.

00:37:23.909 --> 00:37:26.178
We still have to pull out poisonous weeds, right?

00:37:26.879 --> 00:37:29.649
If we don't stop him, even the healthy plants won't grow.

00:37:35.388 --> 00:37:36.689
(Gyeongsangbuk-do Moms' Chatroom)

00:37:36.689 --> 00:37:37.957
(Studying abroad in countryside)

00:37:37.957 --> 00:37:39.792
(I moved to the countryside for my child to get into college.)

00:37:39.792 --> 00:37:41.327
(I think that was a good decision.)

00:37:41.327 --> 00:37:43.562
(Are there many families who move for the rural admission track?)

00:37:44.830 --> 00:37:45.931
Rural admission track?

00:37:49.769 --> 00:37:50.703
Here you are.

00:38:01.747 --> 00:38:04.850
It's not easy finding a nice place in Seoul from here, right?

00:38:06.319 --> 00:38:10.222
If things really don't work out,

00:38:10.222 --> 00:38:12.458
would you like to look into Australia or some other country?

00:38:16.395 --> 00:38:19.498
I think Ji Sang needs to stay here.

00:38:19.932 --> 00:38:22.535
Unlike Ji Cheon, puberty is hitting him hard.

00:38:23.169 --> 00:38:24.904
At this rate,

00:38:25.371 --> 00:38:27.673
Ji Sang won't be accepted to any universities.

00:38:27.673 --> 00:38:28.774
He's such a headache.

00:38:41.020 --> 00:38:41.887
Ji Sang.

00:38:43.356 --> 00:38:44.457
Should we talk over there?

00:38:49.729 --> 00:38:52.064
It's called the rural admission track.

00:38:52.498 --> 00:38:54.667
Once Ji Sang has lived here for a few years, he'll qualify for it.

00:38:55.401 --> 00:38:58.704
We'll stay here with you until you have to go back.

00:38:58.704 --> 00:38:59.872
When the time comes for you to go back,

00:39:00.206 --> 00:39:01.707
we'll decide what to do then.

00:39:02.675 --> 00:39:04.010
As for you,

00:39:04.577 --> 00:39:06.545
just focus on escaping this place quickly.

00:39:08.314 --> 00:39:09.515
When it comes to the kids' education,

00:39:09.915 --> 00:39:12.118
there's no consultant better than you, Cho Mi Ryeo.

00:39:15.821 --> 00:39:17.823
About our car...

00:39:17.823 --> 00:39:21.394
I think we should get something for farming instead.

00:39:21.394 --> 00:39:23.229
Yes, let's sell it quickly.

00:39:23.429 --> 00:39:25.498
It's too big to drive around here anyway.

00:39:25.498 --> 00:39:27.166
The kids can take the school bus.

00:39:27.166 --> 00:39:28.601
Are you really okay with this?

00:39:28.601 --> 00:39:29.802
Yes, I am.

00:39:29.802 --> 00:39:31.470
- Are you sure? - Yes.

00:39:31.470 --> 00:39:32.605
Hurry up.

00:39:34.473 --> 00:39:37.310
(Conscience mirror)

00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:45.084
Mr. Seong.

00:39:52.792 --> 00:39:54.827
This is the last time.

00:39:55.661 --> 00:39:57.096
I think this is just the beginning.

00:39:57.096 --> 00:39:58.998
I'm too scared to do this.

00:40:03.336 --> 00:40:05.938
They say this place pays better than the ones in apps.

00:40:11.777 --> 00:40:12.712
He's gone.

00:40:16.515 --> 00:40:18.250
Have you built a seedling nursery yet?

00:40:19.752 --> 00:40:23.089
I don't have a lot of time. Is it really necessary to build one?

00:40:24.490 --> 00:40:25.558
I knew you'd say that.

00:40:26.425 --> 00:40:27.460
Follow me.

00:40:33.032 --> 00:40:35.234
A seedling nursery is very important.

00:40:35.668 --> 00:40:36.836
If you plant seeds directly without raising seedlings first,

00:40:36.836 --> 00:40:39.071
it may seem easy at first, but it'll be much harder later.

00:40:40.806 --> 00:40:44.343
You have to be even more careful with this.

00:40:45.378 --> 00:40:47.513
If you get caught, I'm dead.

00:40:48.047 --> 00:40:49.448
Thank you so much, Mr. Wang.

00:40:50.249 --> 00:40:51.283
I won't forget this.

00:40:58.591 --> 00:41:01.060
(Yeonri-ri Project)

00:41:01.060 --> 00:41:04.163
(3-1. Buy a farming vehicle)

00:41:19.945 --> 00:41:21.314
Let's see.

00:41:21.314 --> 00:41:23.215
(4. Build a seedling nursery)

00:41:23.215 --> 00:41:24.417
This is...

00:41:25.985 --> 00:41:26.886
This.

00:41:27.820 --> 00:41:30.122
And the joint is that one.

00:41:44.904 --> 00:41:47.239
If you plant it, it'll grow.

00:42:03.422 --> 00:42:04.357
Hey.

00:42:07.660 --> 00:42:08.694
What?

00:42:14.066 --> 00:42:15.901
(Red cabbage, anthocyanin)

00:42:23.109 --> 00:42:24.010
Behold.

00:42:24.677 --> 00:42:26.112
I did it.

00:42:26.912 --> 00:42:29.815
Now it's your turn to do the work.

00:42:31.484 --> 00:42:35.888
This is the historic beginning of Seong Tae Hun napa cabbage.

00:42:46.432 --> 00:42:47.333
A nosebleed.

00:42:48.801 --> 00:42:51.103
(D-28)

00:43:01.881 --> 00:43:02.948
Honey.

00:43:02.948 --> 00:43:04.750
- I'm off. - I don't want to eat.

00:43:04.750 --> 00:43:06.152
You must eat before you go.

00:43:10.990 --> 00:43:12.391
(D-25)

00:43:25.471 --> 00:43:27.139
(D-20)

00:43:32.979 --> 00:43:35.681
Honey. Can you take them to school?

00:43:35.681 --> 00:43:38.317
I'm busy. You take them.

00:43:38.317 --> 00:43:39.385
Get up right now!

00:43:41.654 --> 00:43:42.688
Why won't they sprout?

00:43:49.929 --> 00:43:51.897
(D-18)

00:44:03.309 --> 00:44:05.578
Why won't they sprout?

00:44:17.189 --> 00:44:19.692
Why am I not seeing any sprouts?

00:44:20.760 --> 00:44:22.261
Is the soil really the problem?

00:44:56.495 --> 00:44:57.396
What's this?

00:44:58.597 --> 00:44:59.765
It reeks.

00:45:01.300 --> 00:45:02.601
It's bird poop.

00:45:06.172 --> 00:45:07.173
Bird poop?

00:45:09.308 --> 00:45:10.209
Poop?

00:45:36.068 --> 00:45:36.936
It's poop.

00:46:03.529 --> 00:46:05.231
I'm sorry, guys. Just this once.

00:46:05.831 --> 00:46:07.433
Please let me use it this once.

00:46:07.933 --> 00:46:09.702
Calm down. Quiet.

00:47:11.330 --> 00:47:13.633
(3. Get compost and fertilizer)

00:47:17.937 --> 00:47:19.305
That smells good.

00:47:21.574 --> 00:47:22.441
Smell?

00:47:24.443 --> 00:47:25.378
What's this?

00:47:28.280 --> 00:47:29.215
What's this?

00:47:31.450 --> 00:47:32.551
What is this smell?

00:47:38.324 --> 00:47:39.659
What is this?

00:47:39.659 --> 00:47:40.793
Who helped you?

00:47:47.600 --> 00:47:48.634
I did it.

00:47:49.201 --> 00:47:51.203
I pooped all this by myself.

00:47:51.203 --> 00:47:52.338
Fart.

00:47:54.874 --> 00:47:56.108
Take that.

00:47:58.711 --> 00:48:01.847
It must hurt down there.

00:48:02.782 --> 00:48:03.749
I'm getting close.

00:48:06.986 --> 00:48:11.023
(Simwoo Elementary and Middle School)

00:48:27.773 --> 00:48:29.108
What?

00:48:29.108 --> 00:48:30.109
Ji Cheon.

00:48:33.079 --> 00:48:35.715
Did you apply for the kitchen assistant position?

00:48:35.715 --> 00:48:36.882
I didn't think you'd do it.

00:48:36.882 --> 00:48:38.851
I wouldn't say I applied for it.

00:48:39.685 --> 00:48:40.586
I just...

00:48:40.953 --> 00:48:43.723
Since Ji Sang and Ji Gu attend this school, I thought it'd be nice.

00:48:43.723 --> 00:48:44.757
I was just curious.

00:48:44.757 --> 00:48:45.958
When you're curious,

00:48:45.958 --> 00:48:47.460
the quickest way is to experience it yourself.

00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:49.128
What?

00:49:00.206 --> 00:49:01.240
Start with this.

00:49:01.240 --> 00:49:03.609
There is a riot when the kids here get hungry.

00:49:03.609 --> 00:49:04.443
Hurry up.

00:49:04.443 --> 00:49:05.845
Well...

00:49:05.845 --> 00:49:08.781
Wash the potatoes and young radishes really well.

00:49:08.781 --> 00:49:10.049
Scrub them hard so there's no dirt left.

00:49:10.049 --> 00:49:12.184
Then wash the trays.

00:49:20.593 --> 00:49:22.561
Cafe Sunny.

00:49:23.462 --> 00:49:25.164
From the three-way intersection...

00:49:26.232 --> 00:49:28.467
From the three-way intersection...

00:49:29.735 --> 00:49:31.270
Over there.

00:49:31.904 --> 00:49:32.805
Okay.

00:49:37.943 --> 00:49:40.846
What kind of consulting do you need?

00:49:41.747 --> 00:49:42.882
I don't know.

00:49:43.482 --> 00:49:45.951
The village chief is getting in the way of everything.

00:49:45.951 --> 00:49:48.354
I don't know why he hates me so much.

00:49:48.854 --> 00:49:49.689
Then...

00:49:50.056 --> 00:49:52.325
I'll deal with the Women's Association first.

00:49:57.063 --> 00:50:00.800
(Cafe Sunny)

00:50:08.407 --> 00:50:10.009
Hello.

00:50:11.277 --> 00:50:12.478
Goodness.

00:50:12.478 --> 00:50:17.550
So this is the cafe you run, Ms. Nam.

00:50:18.284 --> 00:50:21.354
The cafe is so cozy.

00:50:22.355 --> 00:50:24.724
A cafe is all about the taste of its coffee,

00:50:24.724 --> 00:50:26.125
not its atmosphere.

00:50:31.664 --> 00:50:35.301
I'll have an iced latte.

00:50:35.301 --> 00:50:36.902
Okay.

00:50:37.870 --> 00:50:39.372
A latte.

00:50:42.675 --> 00:50:44.310
Please have a seat and wait.

00:50:44.510 --> 00:50:45.444
Okay.

00:50:50.016 --> 00:50:52.585
It's so cozy and nice.

00:50:55.855 --> 00:50:57.056
A picture.

00:51:03.529 --> 00:51:04.530
Welcome.

00:51:09.502 --> 00:51:10.403
This is her daughter?

00:51:14.473 --> 00:51:15.474
Your daughter...

00:51:16.275 --> 00:51:17.810
She's very pretty.

00:51:20.212 --> 00:51:23.949
She's the smartest girl in Yeonri-ri.

00:51:25.217 --> 00:51:28.454
She was first in her class all through school.

00:51:28.454 --> 00:51:30.690
My oldest was first in his class too.

00:51:30.990 --> 00:51:32.825
How old is your daughter?

00:51:32.825 --> 00:51:34.794
My oldest son is a college student.

00:51:35.528 --> 00:51:37.596
I hope they can be friends.

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:41.934
Your son...

00:51:42.635 --> 00:51:45.838
He's been wandering around town lately.

00:51:45.838 --> 00:51:48.274
Like he's unemployed.

00:51:53.546 --> 00:51:57.183
Medical school is very hard during the semester,

00:51:57.183 --> 00:51:59.418
so I told him to rest while he is staying here.

00:51:59.885 --> 00:52:02.922
Young people need to learn to rest...

00:52:02.922 --> 00:52:06.025
so they can rest properly when they really need it.

00:52:37.923 --> 00:52:40.292
I came to talk to you, Bo Mi.

00:52:50.269 --> 00:52:52.571
You are all here.

00:52:52.571 --> 00:52:54.440
I'll have my usual.

00:52:55.207 --> 00:52:56.542
It better be buy two, get one free.

00:52:56.542 --> 00:52:57.643
I'm here too.

00:52:58.077 --> 00:52:59.979
Iced Americano. Not too strong.

00:52:59.979 --> 00:53:01.580
Medium strength Americano. Okay.

00:53:03.249 --> 00:53:04.917
There's something to discuss for the Women's Association meeting.

00:53:06.152 --> 00:53:07.353
The Women's Association?

00:53:09.388 --> 00:53:12.224
I'll join too.

00:53:13.559 --> 00:53:15.761
I haven't introduced myself yet.

00:53:15.761 --> 00:53:16.896
Hello.

00:53:16.896 --> 00:53:19.565
I'm Cho Mi Ryeo, who just moved here.

00:53:21.000 --> 00:53:22.635
I thought you said you wouldn't join.

00:53:24.437 --> 00:53:27.206
I had just moved here back then,

00:53:27.206 --> 00:53:28.741
so I was overwhelmed.

00:53:28.741 --> 00:53:31.477
I'm a resident of Yeonri-ri as long as I live here,

00:53:31.644 --> 00:53:34.313
so if there's work to do, I should be part of it too.

00:53:36.115 --> 00:53:38.117
By the way, you are so classy.

00:53:38.117 --> 00:53:39.285
You're drinking an iced Americano.

00:53:40.152 --> 00:53:42.388
Iced Americano...

00:53:42.388 --> 00:53:44.023
Are you saying that...

00:53:44.590 --> 00:53:46.959
old country ladies should just drink...

00:53:46.959 --> 00:53:48.060
cheap instant coffee?

00:53:48.060 --> 00:53:49.795
No, not at all.

00:53:50.363 --> 00:53:52.131
I'm diabetic.

00:53:52.832 --> 00:53:54.266
So I drink lattes...

00:53:54.266 --> 00:53:56.602
without any syrup.

00:53:57.737 --> 00:53:59.105
I have low blood sugar.

00:54:00.439 --> 00:54:03.342
Diabetes is manageable as long as you take your meds properly.

00:54:08.381 --> 00:54:10.716
So, you're joining the Women's Association?

00:54:12.618 --> 00:54:13.586
Deok Rae.

00:54:13.819 --> 00:54:16.722
She hasn't even paid the membership fee yet.

00:54:16.722 --> 00:54:17.990
She can just pay it.

00:54:17.990 --> 00:54:21.193
Have you ever seen anyone from Mat Story last more than two months here?

00:54:21.193 --> 00:54:22.061
That's right.

00:54:22.061 --> 00:54:25.264
You still don't get it, even after what they did to you?

00:54:25.264 --> 00:54:27.133
She shouldn't be allowed to join.

00:54:27.133 --> 00:54:28.968
She must wait at least a year.

00:55:08.174 --> 00:55:09.108
What?

00:55:09.742 --> 00:55:10.810
What's wrong with her?

00:55:11.544 --> 00:55:12.878
Are you all right?

00:55:13.312 --> 00:55:14.947
Ms. Cho Mi Ryeo. What is it?

00:55:14.947 --> 00:55:16.315
What is it, Ms. Cho?

00:55:16.315 --> 00:55:18.150
Your purse? What?

00:55:18.150 --> 00:55:19.151
This?

00:55:19.151 --> 00:55:20.319
What's wrong with her?

00:55:24.256 --> 00:55:25.124
Ji Cheon.

00:55:26.759 --> 00:55:27.793
He's not here.

00:55:29.167 --> 00:55:33.464
You need to integrate sin squared from zero to eight.

00:55:39.005 --> 00:55:39.905
Ji Cheon.

00:55:39.905 --> 00:55:40.840
Mom.

00:55:41.907 --> 00:55:44.210
Where are they? Mom.

00:55:44.210 --> 00:55:45.311
Come on.

00:55:45.678 --> 00:55:47.279
Why isn't she answering her phone these days?

00:55:50.316 --> 00:55:51.217
Is she busy or something?

00:55:57.256 --> 00:55:58.090
What?

00:56:01.293 --> 00:56:03.696
What is this? What?

00:56:03.696 --> 00:56:05.731
Carol.

00:56:05.731 --> 00:56:08.234
Who is this punk?

00:56:08.234 --> 00:56:09.001
Come on.

00:56:11.704 --> 00:56:13.839
Please leave your message after the tone.

00:56:14.774 --> 00:56:17.743
I knew this would happen.

00:56:17.743 --> 00:56:18.944
What is it, Ji Sang?

00:56:19.145 --> 00:56:20.413
What's wrong?

00:56:22.815 --> 00:56:24.850
Seong Ji Gu. Do you like it here?

00:56:24.850 --> 00:56:25.885
Are you going to keep living here?

00:56:26.419 --> 00:56:28.587
Do you even understand what the kids here are saying?

00:56:30.723 --> 00:56:31.557
No.

00:56:32.391 --> 00:56:34.293
Let's get out of here. Now's our chance.

00:56:35.161 --> 00:56:36.362
Think carefully.

00:56:36.829 --> 00:56:38.898
If you stay here, your grades will drop too.

00:56:40.800 --> 00:56:42.101
Our passports.

00:56:44.670 --> 00:56:45.504
Ji Sang.

00:56:48.407 --> 00:56:50.176
- Your purse? Your purse? - Are you okay?

00:56:50.176 --> 00:56:51.911
What? This?

00:56:51.911 --> 00:56:53.312
What's wrong?

00:56:53.879 --> 00:56:55.748
Here. Here.

00:56:55.748 --> 00:56:56.882
What's wrong with her?

00:56:57.450 --> 00:56:58.451
What's wrong?

00:57:00.286 --> 00:57:01.253
My goodness.

00:57:02.154 --> 00:57:04.056
Seeing how she carries the meds with her,

00:57:04.056 --> 00:57:05.825
- this must be a chronic condition. - A chronic condition?

00:57:05.825 --> 00:57:06.926
Ms. Cho Mi Ryeo.

00:57:06.926 --> 00:57:09.795
Do you think you can take your meds?

00:57:09.795 --> 00:57:10.896
Ms. Cho Mi Ryeo.

00:57:11.197 --> 00:57:12.465
Call 911.

00:57:13.499 --> 00:57:16.469
- Get a grip, Ms. Cho. - Are you okay?

00:57:16.469 --> 00:57:18.371
Ms. Cho.

00:57:26.245 --> 00:57:27.146
Goodness.

00:57:32.251 --> 00:57:34.020
I'm scared, Ji Sang.

00:57:53.339 --> 00:57:55.107
Why won't they go in?

00:57:55.441 --> 00:57:57.076
Let's get on a plane and go to Toronto.

00:57:57.643 --> 00:57:59.879
What else can Mom and Dad do? They will come after us.

00:58:01.947 --> 00:58:04.183
Do you have money? What about your passport?

00:58:04.717 --> 00:58:06.886
Will they even sell you a ticket without a guardian?

00:58:06.886 --> 00:58:08.220
I don't care. I'm going.

00:58:09.588 --> 00:58:11.957
To be honest, I was going to run away to Seoul or Toronto by myself,

00:58:12.491 --> 00:58:14.627
but I will give you a chance because I feel bad for you.

00:58:15.661 --> 00:58:17.563
Come with me if you want. If not, forget it.

00:58:18.364 --> 00:58:19.398
You're on your own.

00:58:24.670 --> 00:58:25.604
Ji Sang.

00:58:27.573 --> 00:58:28.407
Ji Sang.

00:58:29.408 --> 00:58:30.576
Don't go.

00:58:31.544 --> 00:58:32.478
Ji Sang.

00:58:34.580 --> 00:58:35.881
What do I do?

00:58:43.823 --> 00:58:46.292
Wait for me, Ji Sang.

00:58:55.401 --> 00:59:00.973
(Wife)

00:59:17.490 --> 00:59:18.524
It's soft and fluffy.

00:59:21.127 --> 00:59:22.895
This is what you call a human victory.

00:59:44.517 --> 00:59:46.552
They sprouted. They sprouted.

00:59:48.587 --> 00:59:50.323
I see cabbage sprouts.

00:59:54.960 --> 00:59:56.262
Do you see that, Mr. Choi?

00:59:56.862 --> 00:59:58.364
I did it, Mr. Choi.

01:00:00.166 --> 01:00:01.901
This land isn't dead.

01:00:02.335 --> 01:00:03.235
They sprouted.

01:00:03.469 --> 01:00:04.303
Dad.

01:00:05.004 --> 01:00:05.838
Dad.

01:00:06.372 --> 01:00:08.274
Ji Cheon. Look.

01:00:09.175 --> 01:00:11.143
They sprouted. The cabbage sprouted.

01:00:12.845 --> 01:00:13.746
Dad.

01:00:14.847 --> 01:00:17.717
Ji Sang and Ji Gu are missing.

01:00:20.119 --> 01:00:20.953
What?

01:00:42.708 --> 01:00:43.609
At that moment,

01:00:46.078 --> 01:00:48.614
I was mistaken and thought I had brought life to this land.

01:00:50.583 --> 01:00:52.218
But I hadn't sprouted cabbage...

01:00:53.085 --> 01:00:55.187
I had pressed the switch

01:00:55.187 --> 01:00:57.590
of a time bomb that would blow up the rest of my life.

01:01:26.952 --> 01:01:29.955
(Cabbage Your Life)

01:01:29.955 --> 01:01:31.891
We're treating this as a runaway case.

01:01:31.891 --> 01:01:34.593
What? Our kids ran away?

01:01:34.593 --> 01:01:36.295
My brother is my guardian,

01:01:36.295 --> 01:01:37.496
so I'll go bring him here.

01:01:37.863 --> 01:01:39.665
Ji Gu. Ji Gu.

01:01:39.999 --> 01:01:41.100
Ji Gu.

01:01:41.100 --> 01:01:42.735
- Ji Gu. - Seong Ji Sang.

01:01:43.035 --> 01:01:44.203
Seong Ji Gu.

01:01:44.637 --> 01:01:45.671
What is this?

01:01:45.671 --> 01:01:46.572
My goodness.

01:01:47.139 --> 01:01:48.674
Honey, are you sick?

01:01:48.674 --> 01:01:50.443
I must plow the field.

01:01:50.443 --> 01:01:51.610
Plow the field?

01:01:51.610 --> 01:01:53.346
What? His wife is plowing the field.

01:01:54.580 --> 01:01:57.350
To be honest, I have a disease.

01:01:57.350 --> 01:01:58.351
A butting-in disease.

01:01:58.351 --> 01:02:00.152
I can't stop looking.

01:02:00.152 --> 01:02:02.621
I think I'll become fond of this place even more.

